{"changes":["eka-core/runtime/capture.go: `Similarity` now reduces each token to the set of its plausible plural-insensitive stems (`stems`) and computes token-set Jaccard where a token matches when its stem sets intersect. `stemGroups` drops repeated readings so a title cannot inflate its own overlap; `overlap` counts each token at most once and is symmetric.","eka-core/runtime/capture.go: the Levenshtein fallback and its gate (`len(ta) \u003c= 2 || len(tb) \u003c= 2`) are unchanged. Its job narrows to genuine typos in short titles, which is what keeps long prefix-sharing titles apart.","eka-core/runtime/capture.go: three ambiguity guards in the stemmer, each because the naive rule re-created the same duplicate-draft bug one word class over — `-ches`/`-shes` returns both readings (`watches` is watch+es, `caches` is cache+s); a trailing `s` after `u`/`i` is not stripped (`status`, `virus`, `analysis` are Latin singulars); one pass never iterated, because iterating produced non-words like `statu`.","Known limitation, documented in the code rather than fixed: `-ses` keeps a single reading, so `cases` lands on `cas` and never agrees with `case`. Resolving it means deciding case+s vs cas+es on every `-ses` token (`bases`, `buses`, `phases`, `releases`) — a dictionary question, not a heuristic one. The miss costs a duplicate draft; a wrong merge loses work, so erring toward the miss is deliberate."],"role":"implementation","summary":"Replaced the dedupe similarity metric so singular and plural forms of the same title score as identical at any title length. Owner chose to change the metric rather than widen the fallback gate; tokens are deliberately unweighted because there is no corpus of captured titles to derive IDF from, so a weight would be an invented parameter, and the code comment says so rather than leaving the omission looking like an oversight.","tests":["eka-core runtime/dedupe_test.go: `TestSimilarityPluralsDedupe` replaces `TestSimilarityLongTitleEditsDoNotDedupe`, which had pinned the defect; it now asserts plural dedupe at one, two, three and four tokens, including `fix login cache`/`fix login caches` (three tokens, no fallback available) and `watch the queue`/`watches the queue` for the other side of the `-ches` ambiguity.","eka-core runtime/dedupe_test.go: `TestSimilarityDifferingLongTitlesDoNotDedupe` guards the over-merge direction — `fix login bug in auth` vs `fix login bug in billing` must not dedupe.","eka-core runtime/dedupe_test.go: `TestSimilarityStemmingKeepsDistinctWordsApart` asserts exact stem values (`status`-\u003e`status`, `statuses`-\u003e`status`, `class`/`classes`-\u003e`class`, `analysis`/`analyses`-\u003e`analysis`, `caches` keeps both readings) and that no nonsense stem is produced.","Non-vacuous proof: with the previous single-form stemmer restored, the new tests report `fix login cache`/`fix login caches` = 0.5 and `stems(\"status\") = [statu]`.","go test ./runtime/ -count=1 -\u003e ok (177s). go test ./exchange/ -count=1 -\u003e ok. go test ./... -count=1 -\u003e all 13 packages ok. gofmt -l runtime/ empty, go vet ./runtime/ clean."]}